# Documentation Standards for Auditability

These standards ensure that third-party auditors can understand the **intent** behind code, not just its function. Proper documentation is a security and compliance requirement.

## 1. JSDoc Requirements

**ALL exported functions MUST have complete JSDoc documentation.**

### Required JSDoc Tags

| Tag | Required For | Description |
|-----|-------------|-------------|
| `@description` | All functions | What the function does |
| `@param` | All parameters | Type and purpose of each parameter |
| `@returns` | All non-void | What gets returned |
| `@throws` | Error conditions | What errors can be thrown |
| `@security` | Auth/security code | Security implications |
| `@audit` | Audit-logged functions | What gets logged to audit tables |

### Complete JSDoc Template

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Complete JSDoc for exported function
/**
 * Creates a new task and assigns it to a user within a foundry.
 * 
 * @description Creates a task with proper foundry isolation, validates 
 * user permissions, and logs the creation to the audit trail.
 * 
 * @param {Object} params - Task creation parameters
 * @param {string} params.foundryId - The foundry this task belongs to
 * @param {string} params.title - Task title (max 200 chars)
 * @param {string} params.assigneeId - User ID to assign task to
 * @param {string} [params.description] - Optional task description
 * 
 * @returns {Promise<Task>} The created task with generated ID
 * 
 * @throws {UnauthorizedError} If user lacks task.create permission
 * @throws {NotFoundError} If foundry or assignee doesn't exist
 * @throws {ValidationError} If title exceeds 200 characters
 * 
 * @security Requires authenticated user with foundry membership
 * @audit Logs task_created event with task_id, foundry_id, created_by
 * 
 * @example
 * const task = await createTask({
 *   foundryId: 'foundry_123',
 *   title: 'Review quarterly report',
 *   assigneeId: 'user_456'
 * })
 */
export async function createTask(params: CreateTaskParams): Promise<Task> {
  // AUTH: Verify user has permission to create tasks in this foundry
  await requirePermission(params.foundryId, 'task.create')
  
  // VALIDATION: Ensure title meets constraints
  if (params.title.length > 200) {
    throw new ValidationError('Title must be 200 characters or less')
  }
  
  // ... implementation
}

// ❌ WRONG - Missing JSDoc entirely
export async function createTask(params: CreateTaskParams): Promise<Task> {
  // No documentation - auditor cannot understand intent
}

// ❌ WRONG - Incomplete JSDoc
/**
 * Creates a task.
 */
export async function createTask(params: CreateTaskParams): Promise<Task> {
  // Missing @param, @returns, @throws, @security, @audit
}
```

